  "issue_date": "2024-07-19",
  "report_week": "29",
  "report_period": "Week 29 (12th Jul to 19th Jul 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Oldendorff Carriers committed their Post Panamax \"Claas Oldendorff\" 95/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Singaporean interests at region USD 27 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Van Gogh\" 95/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in late May at USD 25 mill. Following the acquisition of the Kamsarmax \"Livia Rose\" 81/2018 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2028, DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) three weeks ago at USD 35,7 mill, clients of HMM have now bought the one-year-younger \"BW Kobe\" 81/2019 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 07/2029, DD 07/2027, BWTS fitted) at USD 37 mill. The Panamax \"Glory Trader\" 77/2004 CSBC, Taiwan (SS 08/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 11,7 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Pan Eldorado\" 77/2004 CSBC, Taiwan (SS/DD 04/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in November at USD 8,8 mill. On the Supramax sector, Japanese owners committed their \"Royal Samurai\" 58/2010 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 17,3 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"Rego\" 58/2009 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 08/2029, DD 02/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 16,5 mill. Moreover, Chinese owners committed the \"Seacon Yantai\" 57/2010 Cosco, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to clients of PT Primatama Energi Mandiri at mid-high USD 13 mill. H Vogemann committed their Handysize \"Voge Mia\" & \"Voge Emma\" 36/2011 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 05/2026 & SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 30,6 mill enbloc, while the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Darya Jamuna\" 36/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 05/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) from Chellaram Shipping was committed at low USD 16 mill.",
    "tankers": "Hafnia Tankers committed their MR2 \"Hafnia Pegasus\" 50/2010 Guangzhou, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 28,5 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Dignity\" 50/2010 Guangzhou, China (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 29 mill. In addition, Coral Shipping committed their \"Daytona\" 47/2005 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) at high USD 17 mill. Remind you that the one-year- older \"Dai Minh\" 47/2004 Onomichi, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in early May at USD 16 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low-mid usd 9,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 23,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K-900K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 18,000 pd for 8/10 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesia trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Trips from Philippines into China were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 180K/200K. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 13,000/14,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K-600K. An Ultramax was reported fixed in the usd 14,500 pd for 3/5 months employment basis delivery India.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. Continental trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
